From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: himax-spi: clamp edge-compensated coordinates within axis bounds

hx_edge_compensate() clamped the right and bottom Q8 grid coordinates to
(HX_COLS - 1) * 256 + 256 (15360) and (HX_ROWS - 1) * 256 + 256 (10240), which
map to output coordinates 2560 and 1600—one unit beyond the maximum axis bounds
of 2559 and 1599 (and -1 after touchscreen-inverted-x). Android's
TouchInputMapper drops initial touch frames outside the axis range, delaying
edge swipes and dropping corner taps.

Clamp the upper Q8 bounds to HX_COLS * 256 - 1 and HX_ROWS * 256 - 1 so output
coordinates stay within 0..2559 and 0..1599.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c
index a1eff6d..d284481 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/hx-algo.c
@@ -1278,11 +1278,15 @@ static void hx_edge_compensate(struct hx_algo *algo, struct hx_contact *ct)
 		ct->x = max_t(s32, ct->x - push, 0);
 	}
 
-	/* Right boundary: distance from last col center */
+	/*
+	 * Right boundary: distance from last col center.  The push stops
+	 * at the last Q8 position of the grid: one further would report one
+	 * past the axis maximum, and Android ignores a touch while it is there.
+	 */
 	dist = (HX_COLS - 1) * 256 + 128 - ct->x;
 	if (dist < blend) {
 		push = push_max * (blend - dist) / blend;
-		ct->x = min_t(s32, ct->x + push, (HX_COLS - 1) * 256 + 256);
+		ct->x = min_t(s32, ct->x + push, HX_COLS * 256 - 1);
 	}
 
 	/* Top boundary */
@@ -1296,7 +1300,7 @@ static void hx_edge_compensate(struct hx_algo *algo, struct hx_contact *ct)
 	dist = (HX_ROWS - 1) * 256 + 128 - ct->y;
 	if (dist < blend) {
 		push = push_max * (blend - dist) / blend;
-		ct->y = min_t(s32, ct->y + push, (HX_ROWS - 1) * 256 + 256);
+		ct->y = min_t(s32, ct->y + push, HX_ROWS * 256 - 1);
 	}
 }
 
